---
version: 2.0.2
title: parse diagnostic: external declaration mistakes
file: ./test/parser_error_test.gleam
test_name: external_errors_rendering_test
---
Source:
module main

external now() -> Int

external Clock from python "clock" {
  now(): Int
  at(zone) -> Int
}

---
error: external declarations name a namespace
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:3:10
  │
3 │ external now() -> Int
  │          ─┬─
  │           ╰─ expected a namespace name such as `Crypto`
  ╰─

Foreign functions are grouped under a namespace that names their language and module.

help: Write `external Crypto from erlang "crypto" { strong_rand_bytes(size: Int) -> BitArray }`.

error: unsupported foreign language
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:5:21
  │
5 │ external Clock from python "clock" {
  │                     ───┬──
  │                        ╰─ `python` is not a supported language
  ╰─

The supported languages are `erlang`, `elixir`, `gleam` and `lfe`.

note: Modules written in any other BEAM language can be called with `erlang` and their module atom.

note: Native code is declared with `native Name from "component" { ... }`.

error: external signatures use `->`
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:6:8
  │
6 │   now(): Int
  │        ┬
  │        ╰─ expected `->` before the result type
  ╰─

External signatures are written `name(parameter: Type) -> Result`.

error: missing parameter type
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:7:6
  │
7 │   at(zone) -> Int
  │      ──┬─
  │        ╰─ `zone` has no type
  ╰─

Every parameter of an external signature needs a type.

help: Write `zone: Type`.

Found 4 errors.

